        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Akira Yoshizawa, Hirohito\n- Concepts: Wet-folding, Shōwa era, Order of the Rising Sun\n\nFacts:\n- Akira Yoshizawa developed the origami technique called wet-folding.\n- Wet-folding uses water to dampen paper so it can be manipulated more easily.\n- In 1983, Emperor Hirohito awarded Akira Yoshizawa the Order of the Rising Sun, 5th class, one of Japan's highest honors.\n- Shōwa was the era name corresponding to Emperor Hirohito's reign.\n- Upon Hirohito's death, Shōwa became the Emperor's own name.",
